# Chat pacing: a burst of say_all lines is spread out by
# rmm.chatInterval (default 1.0 s). The first line goes out at once; the rest
# arrive in order after the .wait, not before the "marker" line.
.join Alice 1
.pacing on
say one
say two
say three
rmm version
.wait 4
# a line over BFV's 63-character limit is split at a word boundary, and the
# second half is paced like any other line
say the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog and keeps running far away
rmm version
.wait 2
# with pacing off (script default) everything is immediate again
.pacing off
say four
say five
rmm version
